#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148730 :tutorial/content "The **faces** of a polyhedron are the polygonal sides that construct it. \n\nLet's consider the triangular prism below.\n\n![](images/4e/4e0550f18e27ad9326b5606f23b502ff6879d2149f5bac5e2fcc829506748f0b.png)\n\nOur triangular prism has $5$ faces:\n\n![](images/ca/cabe6f9d976ad0b577d8a12b22fda051a284416c284b88c90723bbbcbcd0f723.png)\n\nThe **vertices** of a polyhedron are its corners. Our triangular prism has $6$ vertices:\n\n![](images/15/153dffffba0e8e344f667d9b4aa0badbd8b6560bdf731b75b1a3efafd2c2a7cc.png)\n\nThe **edges** of a polyhedron are the straight line segments that connect its vertices. Our triangular prism has $9$ edges:\n\n![](images/b0/b001673f783be6e9cb45fe42375d460fbe5aa760843b02ad480b340641b5c3bc.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "9a0867c3-217a-596d-8426-8bafb724cb53" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2335 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
